# r4tsk feature showcase
#
# A single script touching every feature r4tsk adds on top of plain Skript
# syntax highlighting. Open this file, hover things, and try:
#   - Ctrl+T for workspace symbols, F12 for go-to-definition
#   - hovering a function call, an effect/condition/event, or a color code
#   - the color swatch next to any <#rrggbb> tag below
#
# A few settings-driven features aren't visible as code at all, so they're
# just noted here instead:
#   - r4tsk.customPatterns / "r4tsk: Configure Custom Colored Patterns" - color
#     any regex pattern you define, e.g. an ASCII-art banner comment block.
#   - r4tsk.additionalDocsPaths / "r4tsk: Manage Addon Docs Files..." - merge
#     in an addon's docs.json (SkBee, Skript-GUI, ...) for hover/diagnostics.
#   - r4tsk.docsPath / "r4tsk: Set Core Docs File..." - use your own core
#     docs.json instead of the bundled/auto-downloaded one.
#   - Skript version tracking (status bar item, bottom right) and
#     auto-downloading the matching docs.json - both apply globally, not
#     to any specific line of code.
#   - "You might be thinking of X from Skript Y" - cross-version hover
#     suggestions when something isn't found in your configured version.

# --- JavaDoc-style doc comments -------------------------------------------
# @param/@return/@deprecated are parsed structurally and shown in hover,
# autocomplete and signature help. @param/@return/@deprecated tags are
# colored (not just the surrounding text) - see r4tsk.annotationColors.*.

# Gives a welcome kit to a player and announces it in chat.
#
# @param p the player to give the kit to
# @param announce whether to broadcast a message about it
# @param kit the item type that represents the kit
# @return whether the kit was successfully given
function giveWelcomeKit(p: player, announce: boolean, kit: itemtype) :: boolean:
	give kit to p
	if announce is true:
		broadcast "<#f18d8d>%p% &ljust joined and got a kit!"
	return true

# Calculates a player's payout. Kept only as an example of a deprecated
# function - hover it to see the "⚠️ Deprecated" warning.
#
# @param p the player to calculate the payout for
# @param minutesPlayed how many minutes they've played this session
# @return the payout amount in coins
# @deprecated use economy.calculatePayout() from the new economy addon instead
function calculatePayout(p: player, minutesPlayed: number) :: number:
	set {_base} to minutesPlayed * 2
	if minutesPlayed > 60:
		add 50 to {_base}
	return {_base}

# `local function` - only callable from within this script. Calling it from
# another .sk file wouldn't resolve (correctly), and it can share its name
# with an unrelated local function elsewhere without r4tsk flagging a
# "duplicate function" diagnostic - only a real same-file collision, or two
# *global* functions colliding across files, are actual conflicts.
#
# @param p the player to greet
local function greetLocally(p: player):
	send "<#7fd6ff>Welcome, %p%!" to p

# --- Diagnostics: a deliberately broken doc comment ------------------------
# No `:: type` return declaration on this one, but the @return tag below
# still claims one - r4tsk flags that mismatch as a diagnostic. This is the
# only intentionally "broken" thing in this file.
#
# TODO hook this up to the real logging addon once it's released.
# WARN this still uses the placeholder log format below.
# ! do not remove this until the new logging system ships.
# important: "!" and "important" both trigger the same red highlighting.
#
# @param p the player to log a message for
# @return whether logging succeeded
function logNothing(p: player):
	send "logged" to p

# --- Commands ---------------------------------------------------------------
command /kit:
	permission: r4tsk.example.kit
	description: Gives you the example welcome kit.
	usage: /kit
	trigger:
		giveWelcomeKit(player, true, diamond sword)

# --- Events ------------------------------------------------------------------
on join:
	# Hover "giveWelcomeKit"/"greetLocally"/"logNothing" to see each parsed
	# doc comment: description, per-parameter text, return value, and the
	# deprecation warning where present.
	set {_gotKit} to giveWelcomeKit(player, true, diamond sword)
	greetLocally(player)
	logNothing(player)

on explode:
	# A real event since Skript 1.0 - hover "explode" above to confirm it
	# resolves correctly (it's built from adjacent choice groups internally,
	# `explo(d(e|ing)|sion)`, which r4tsk expands to index "explode"/
	# "exploding"/"explosion" as real words, not meaningless fragments).
	cancel the event

# --- Real pattern-matching hover / diagnostics --------------------------
# Hover any of these lines: r4tsk identifies exactly which effect/condition/
# expression governs it (not just that a keyword coincidentally appears),
# and shows which argument text filled which %placeholder%.
on script load:
	set {_inventory} to inventory with 3 rows
	set {_item} to diamond sword
	add {_item} to {_inventory}

	if {_inventory} contains {_item}:
		broadcast "&aFound it!"

	loop 3 times:
		wait 1 tick

	loop {_inventory}'s items:
		if loop-value is not air:
			send "%loop-value%" to console

	teleport player to {_inventory}'s location
	kill player's target

# --- Minecraft chat colors and hex tags -------------------------------------
# Legacy &-codes and <#rrggbb> hex tags both render live using their actual
# in-game color (not a generic "this is a string" color), following real
# chat rendering rules (a color code resets formatting, format codes stack).
# Hover/click the swatch next to the hex tag below for the color picker.
on script load:
	broadcast "&c&lWarning: &r&7this text is grey and unformatted"
	broadcast "<#ff7ff9>gradient-ready pink <#25dee4>and cyan in one message"

# --- Variables ---------------------------------------------------------------
on script load:
	set {_local} to "scoped to this trigger only"
	set {example::global} to "shared across the whole server"
	set {example::list::1} to "first"
	set {example::list::2} to "second"
	loop {example::list::*}:
		send "%loop-index%: %loop-value%" to console

# --- Deprecated-syntax warning (intentional) ---------------------------------
# `'s nick name`/`'s custom name` have no replacement property in Skript
# 2.13+, so this line still correctly warns - uncomment it to see the
# diagnostic. Compare with `'s name`/`'s display name`, which *are* covered
# by non-deprecated properties now and correctly stay silent.
on script load:
	# set the player's nick name to "Nicky"
	set the player's display name to "<#ffd21c>%player's name%"

# --- Java interop (e.g. Skript-Reflect) doesn't get flagged -----------------
# Dot-chain method calls like `SomeClass.method(...)` or `{_x}.isEmpty()`
# aren't Skript function calls, so r4tsk doesn't flag them as undefined
# functions the way it would a bare `identifier(...)`. Left commented since
# it depends on an addon's actual Java classes, not anything bundled here.
#
# import:
# 	kr.toxicity.model.api.BetterModel
# on script load:
# 	set {_opt} to BetterModel.model("example")
# 	if {_opt}.isEmpty() is true:
# 		stop

# --- Diagnostics playground (commented out - uncomment to see each one) -----
# on script load:
# 	thisFunctionDoesNotExist(player)               # Undefined function 'thisFunctionDoesNotExist'.
# 	giveWelcomeKit(player)                          # Missing required argument 'announce: boolean'.
# 	giveWelcomeKit(player, true, diamond sword, 5)  # Too many arguments: 'giveWelcomeKit' takes 3, got 4.
